# Day 49 — Personal AI Playbook: Turning My AI Habits Into a Consistency System

**Challenge:** ABTalks 60-Day Claude Challenge
**Track:** Personal AI Systems
**Author:** [Vivek Kumar](https://www.linkedin.com/in/vivekdp/)
**Day:** 49 of 60
**Deliverable:** `personal-ai-playbook.html` (single self-contained file), `workflow-library.json`, screenshots

---

## 🎯 Objective

Build a personalised, fully interactive AI playbook — not a prompt collection, but a system of reusable building blocks that combine into whatever the task needs.

The interview step asked what my actual bottleneck is. My answer wasn't "writing prompts is slow." It was:

> **Review #7 and review #21 don't score or phrase the same way — and that's a problem when the whole set gets audited as a body of work.**

That single answer reshaped the build. Everything below is designed for **determinism**, not for flexibility.

